nonprofit-helping-seniors-use-technology-and-won-an-ai-leadership-award/articleshow/133513004.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-hannah-joseph-the-ohio-sophomore-who-pitched-a-nonprofit-helping-seniors-use-technology-and-won-an-ai-leadership-award/articleshow/133513004.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T22:00:32+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133513761,imgsize-68817.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Florida voters have approved $35 million to buy and transform 5.8 miles of underused railroad...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133516926.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Bonita Springs voters have greenlit a $35 million bond aimed at improving the essential rail corridor. This significant investment secures the central portion of the Bonita Estero Rail Trail, effectively bridging a gap within the Florida Gulf Coast Trail. Importantly, this development will enhance connectivity between the Estero and Collier County sections of the trail, with construction anticipated to commence in October following the finalization of the purchase.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/florida-voters-have-approved-35-million-to-buy-and-transform-5-8-miles-of-underused-railroad-into-a-trail-that-will-form-part-of-an-11-4-mile-greenway-and-help-close-a-gap-in-a-planned-400-mile-trail-network/articleshow/133516926.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/florida-voters-have-approved-35-million-to-buy-and-transform-5-8-miles-of-underused-railroad-into-a-trail-that-will-form-part-of-an-11-4-mile-greenway-and-help-close-a-gap-in-a-planned-400-mile-trail-network/articleshow/133516926.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T21:59:49+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133518910,imgsize-1298429.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Mentmore Towers, Batman Begins’ Wayne Manor in Buckinghamshire, could be seized over repairs]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133517166.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The real-life Wayne Manor from Batman Begins, Mentmore Towers in Buckinghamshire, could face compulsory purchase if its owners fail to repair the deteriorating Grade I-listed mansion. According to SWNS, authorities have ordered urgent restoration work and three bat surveys by August 2027. The historic property has suffered damaged roofs, cracks, broken windows and neglect.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/mentmore-towers-batman-begins-wayne-manor-in-buckinghamshire-could-be-seized-as-owners-face-deadline-to-repair-crumbling-mansion-and-conduct-bat-surveys-to-save-historic-property/articleshow/133517166.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/mentmore-towers-batman-begins-wayne-manor-in-buckinghamshire-could-be-seized-as-owners-face-deadline-to-repair-crumbling-mansion-and-conduct-bat-surveys-to-save-historic-property/articleshow/133517166.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T21:21:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133517486,imgsize-196117.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Fortescue suspends senior executive during workplace misconduct probe]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133518327.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.ind