india.indiatimes.com/world/us/zero-self-awareness-indian-origin-professor-slams-viral-video-of-woman-welcoming-mother-at-us-airport-triggering-wheelchair-row/articleshow/133517770.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/zero-self-awareness-indian-origin-professor-slams-viral-video-of-woman-welcoming-mother-at-us-airport-triggering-wheelchair-row/articleshow/133517770.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T21:31:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133518002,imgsize-34988.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Artist turns 600-square-foot cabin into 5,000-square-foot home and living artwork over 37 years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133511745.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Luna Parc in New Jersey began as a 600-square-foot cabin that artist Ricky Boscarino started transforming in 1989. Over the years, he turned it into a 5,000-square-foot, 11-level home and studio filled with artwork, collections and unusual spaces. The property also serves as a teaching space where young local artists learn craft and business skills.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-new-jersey-artist-bought-a-600-square-foot-cabin-in-1989-and-kept-adding-to-it-37-years-later-luna-parc-is-a-5000-square-foot-home-studio-and-living-artwork-still-being-built/articleshow/133511745.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-new-jersey-artist-bought-a-600-square-foot-cabin-in-1989-and-kept-adding-to-it-37-years-later-luna-parc-is-a-5000-square-foot-home-studio-and-living-artwork-still-being-built/articleshow/133511745.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T21:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133512812,imgsize-288190.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1867, New Zealand introduced brown trout for sport fishing; more than 60 million were released]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133515153.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In 1867, British settlers introduced brown trout to New Zealand, intending to enhance sport fishing. This decision led to the release of over sixty million trout, which had devastating effects on local fish populations, resulting in declines and even extinction of some native species. The presence of these invasive fish fundamentally changed stream ecosystems and insect behaviors, making their management a significant conservation challenge even today.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-1867-new-zealand-introduced-brown-trout-for-sport-fishing-more-than-60-million-were-released-by-1921-and-the-invader-later-caused-local-extinctions-and-fragmented-native-fish-populations/articleshow/133515153.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-1867-new-zealand-introduced-brown-trout-for-sport-fishing-more-than-60-million-were-released-by-1921-and-the-invader-later-caused-local-extinctions-and-fragmented-native-fish-populations/articleshow/133515153.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T20:09:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133515463,imgsize-1724655.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Lindsay Clancy trial: Judge rejects mistrial plea after psychologist's Catholic faith remarks]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133515138.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></descriptio