g-her-new-york-home-including-a-100-year-old-family-heirloom-her-husband-dug-through-20000-pounds-of-trash-to-find-them/articleshow/133508387.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/she-accidentally-threw-away-two-rings-while-cleaning-her-new-york-home-including-a-100-year-old-family-heirloom-her-husband-dug-through-20000-pounds-of-trash-to-find-them/articleshow/133508387.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T17:24:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133508645,imgsize-1793554.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Married NYC lawyer getting fired after his video of smooching 29-year-old colleague in Central Park goes viral]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133511548.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/married-nyc-lawyer-getting-fired-after-his-video-of-smooching-29-year-old-colleague-in-central-park-goes-viral/articleshow/133511548.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/married-nyc-lawyer-getting-fired-after-his-video-of-smooching-29-year-old-colleague-in-central-park-goes-viral/articleshow/133511548.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T18:28:04+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133511808,imgsize-77698.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[7,000-year-old beaver bone pit reveals how Europe’s first farmers used animal fur]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133511152.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Near Alsleben, Germany, archaeologists have unearthed a beaver bone pit that dates back 7,000 years. This remarkable find sheds light on the early farming communities and their sophisticated practices in fur exploitation. The arrangement of the bones points to organized hunting activities. Researchers suggest that such evidence indicates that these ancient peoples crafted intricate fur clothing to adapt to their environment.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/archaeologists-found-a-7000-year-old-pit-packed-with-beaver-bones-it-reveals-how-europes-first-farmers-used-animal-fur/articleshow/133511152.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/archaeologists-found-a-7000-year-old-pit-packed-with-beaver-bones-it-reveals-how-europes-first-farmers-used-animal-fur/articleshow/133511152.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T21:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133511300,imgsize-1029733.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1932, an Ohio worker lost his job and began building a rock garden; he spent 12 and his wife...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133510533.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Upon losing his job at the factory, Harry Hartman transformed his passion into a breathtaking folk art garden made from more than 250,000 stones and repurposed materials. For 53 years, his devoted wife Mary cared for this enchanting space until the Kohler Foundation restored it and handed it over to a community non-profit. The garden is now a beautiful destination for public tours, showcasing Harry's visionary artistry.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1932-an-ohio-foundry-worker-lost-his-job-and-began-building-a-rock-garden-he-spent-12-years-creating-hundreds-of-structures-and-his-wife-preserved-it-for-another-53-years/articleshow/133510533.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1932-an-ohio-foundry-worker-lost-his-job-and-began-building-a-rock-garden-he-spent-12-years-creating-hundreds-of-structures-and-his-wife-preserved-it-for-another-53-years/articleshow/133510533.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T18:22:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133511442,imgsize-1723463.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2014, Texas bought 17,351-acre Powderhorn Ranch; 15,000 acres later became a wildlife area]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133508433.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In 2014, a coalition of conservation groups bought 17,351-acre Powderhorn Ranch on the Texas coast for $37.7 million. A major share of the funding came from BP and Transocean penalties linked to the Deepwater Horizon oil spill. Four years later, more than 15,000 acres were transferred to Texas Parks and Wildlife Department as a wildlife management area.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2014-a-texas-coalition-bought-a-17351-acre-coastal-ranch-for-37-7-million-much-of-it-using-deepwater-horizon-restoration-money-15000-acres-later-became-a-wildlife-area-protecting-wetlands-prairie-and-endangered-whooping-crane-habitat/articleshow/133508433.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2014-a-texas-coalition-bought-a-17351-acre-coastal-ranch-for-37-7-million-much-of-it-using-deepwater-horizon-restoration-money-15000-acres-later-became-a-wildlife-area-protecting-wetlands-prairie-and-endangered-whooping-crane-habitat/articleshow/133508433.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T18:17:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/